The following files are third-party code, tested/adapted by Alexandre Matov
but not authored by him:

`Training_DeTraC.m`, `Training_original_classes.m`,
`createLgraphUsingConnections.m`, `findLayersToReplace.m`,
`construct_dataset_B.m`, `extract_features.m`, `Pca_CXR.m`,
`ConfusionMat_MultiClass.m`, `readAndPreprocessImage.m`, `DeTraC_model.ipynb`
-- from the DeTraC codebase, developed by the lab of Mohamed Gaber,
Birmingham City University:

  Abbas, A., Abdelsamea, M.M., Gaber, M.M. "Classification of COVID-19 in
  Chest X-ray Images Using DeTraC Deep Convolutional Neural Network."
  Applied Intelligence 51 (2021): 854-864.
  https://github.com/asmaa4may/DeTraC_COVId19

`cnn.py` is the CNNModule class from the DeepChem library
(deepchem.models.torch_models).

`DeepLearning_Keras.py`, `LogisticRegressionExample.py`,
`XGBoost_Model_test.py`, `kerasMNISTconvnet.R` are adapted from standard
public tutorial/example code for Keras, scikit-learn, XGBoost, and
Keras-in-R, respectively -- not original work.

`CNN_test.py`, `testMNISTconvnet.R`, `mnist_convet.R`, `regressionUmiseq.R`,
`txttojpg.R` are code I wrote.
